 "commands": [
  "bun tools/compile-rivals.mjs --runs 2 --sizes 1000,4000 --twins hashmap,bintrees,strings,json,dyncall,iterchain,ecs",
  "Grail's store before each cold run: grail cache warm (every standard module); Go's GOCACHE holds its standard library, Zig's cache its compiler_rt, and cargo uses the offline registry, so the standard library is warm for every toolchain",
  "one process: GRAIL_JOBS=1, GOMAXPROCS=1 GOFLAGS=-p=1, CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 (make builds one translation unit, so one job); four jobs: the same at 4",
  "Grail: check `grail check main.grl`, build `grail build main.grl`",
  "Go: check `go vet .`, build `go build -o syn .`",
  "Zig: check `zig build-exe -fno-emit-bin main.zig`, build `zig build-exe -O Debug main.zig`",
  "C: check `clang -fsyntax-only main.c`, build `make -s`",
  "C++: check `clang++ -std=c++20 -fsyntax-only main.cpp`, build `make -s`",
  "Rust: check `cargo check --offline -q`, build `cargo build --offline -q`",
  "C and C++: one translation unit per program and a one-target Makefile (CFLAGS -O0 -g, CXXFLAGS -std=c++20 -O0 -g, LDFLAGS -fuse-ld=lld); nothing changed is make finding the target up to date",
  "edit: the generated programs change one constant in one function body; a twin gets one statement added to main"
 ],
